<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theodorus of Samos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theodorus of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samo">Samos</a> was a Greek architect, sculptor and metalworker of the 6th century BCE. Ancient writers credit him, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhoecus">Rhoecus</a>, with the great temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hera">Hera</a> on Samos and with pioneering the casting of bronze statues, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> names him as the maker of the ring of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polycrates">Polycrates</a>. He was also said to have advised on the foundations of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temple-of-artemis">Temple of Artemis at Ephesus</a>.</p></div>
